msgstr "鑑於 Qubes OS 的技術特性，先前具備 Linux 經驗會有所幫助。"

#: ../../../introduction/intro.rst:66 bd5a77ebf1ba4a6bb36ca41d0f14d345
msgid "Why Qubes OS?"
msgstr "為什麼選擇 Qubes OS？"

#: ../../../introduction/intro.rst:69 17ada8a9a07249e18f93d46023d27ccf
msgid "Physical isolation is a given safeguard that the digital world lacks"
msgstr "實體隔離是數位世界所缺乏的既有防護措施"

#: ../../../introduction/intro.rst:71 b63f8d9805b4410eba3022acbf7c58b8
msgid ""
"Throughout our lives, we engage in various activities, such as going to "
"school, working, voting, taking care of our families, and visiting with "
"friends. These activities are spatially and temporally bound: They happen in "
"isolation from one another, in their own compartments, which often represent "
"an essential safeguard, as in the case of voting."
msgstr ""
"在我們的一生中，我們從事各種活動，例如上學、工作、投票、照顧家人以及與朋友聚"
"會。這些活動在空間和時間上是受限的：它們彼此隔離地發生，各有其獨立的隔間，而"
"這些隔間往往代表了一種基本的防護措施，投票就是一個例子。"

#: ../../../introduction/intro.rst:77 3f2d187b21c94fafb821eb22a1cdf2d2
msgid ""
"In our digital lives, the situation is quite different: All of our "
"activities typically happen on a single device. This causes us to worry "
"about whether it's safe to click on a link or install an app, since being "
"hacked imperils our entire digital existence."
msgstr ""
"在我們的數位生活中，情況則大不相同：我們所有的活動通常都在單一裝置上進行。這"
"讓我們擔心點擊連結或安裝應用程式是否安全，因為一旦被駭，整個數位生活都將陷入"
"危險。"

#: ../../../introduction/intro.rst:82 61b64e55072f4c59bf16a13ec3e182e2
msgid ""
"Qubes eliminates this concern by allowing us to divide a device into many "
"compartments, much as we divide a physical building into many rooms. Better "
"yet, it allows us to create new compartments whenever we need them, and it "
"gives us sophisticated tools for securely managing our activities and data "
"across these compartments."
msgstr ""
"Qubes 消除了這種擔憂，它允許我們將裝置劃分為多個隔間，就像我們將一棟實體建築"
"劃分為許多房間一樣。更棒的是，它讓我們可以隨時建立新的隔間，並提供精密的工具"
"來安全管理跨越這些隔間的活動和資料。"

#: ../../../introduction/intro.rst:88 f1f0f38f215740718e217408136779ce
msgid "Qube manager"
msgstr "Qube 管理員"

#: ../../../introduction/intro.rst:93 7bebe6e8dc2148229daee78715482429
msgid "Qubes allows you to compartmentalize your digital life"
msgstr "Qubes 讓您能夠將數位生活隔間化"

#: ../../../introduction/intro.rst:95 1195910d69ce4681a84977e1b9d74d2a
msgid ""
"Many of us are initially surprised to learn that our devices do not support "
"the kind of secure compartmentalization that our lives demand, and we're "
"disappointed that software vendors rely on generic defenses that repeatedly "
"succumb to new attacks."
msgstr ""
"我們許多人最初驚訝地發現，我們的裝置並不支援我們生活所需的那種安全隔間化，而"
"且我們對軟體供應商依賴那些反覆被新型攻擊擊潰的通用防禦措施感到失望。"

#: ../../../introduction/intro.rst:100 96cd2b5ebab647f49ebae18a0f824e36
msgid ""
"In building Qubes, our working assumption is that all software contains "
"bugs. Not only that, but in their stampeding rush to meet deadlines, the "
"world's stressed-out software developers are pumping out new code at a "
"staggering rate - far faster than the comparatively smaller population of "
"security experts could ever hope to analyze it for vulnerabilities, much "
"less fix everything. Rather than pretend that we can prevent these "
"inevitable vulnerabilities from being exploited, we've designed Qubes under "
"the assumption that they **will** be exploited. It's only a matter of time "
"until the next zero-day attack."
msgstr ""
"在打造 Qubes 的過程中，我們的基本假設是所有軟體都存在缺陷。不僅如此，在趕赴截"
"止日期的匆忙腳步中，全球備受壓力的軟體開發人員正以驚人的速度產出新程式碼——其"
"速度遠遠超過相對少數的安全專家能夠分析漏洞的速度，更不用說修復所有問題了。我"
"們不會假裝能夠防止這些不可避免的漏洞被利用，而是基於它們\\ **將會**\\ 被利用"
"的假設來設計 Qubes。下一次零日攻擊只是時間問題。"

#: ../../../introduction/intro.rst:110 babc07a8b3214ccea8b1c3d94f210d17
msgid ""
"In light of this sobering reality, Qubes takes an eminently practical "
"approach: confine, control, and contain the damage. It allows you to keep "
"valuable data separate from risky activities, preventing cross-"
"contamination. This means you can do everything on the same physical "
"computer without having to worry about a single successful cyberattack "
"taking down your entire digital life in one fell swoop. In fact, Qubes has "
"`distinct advantages over physical air gaps <https://invisiblethingslab.com/"
"resources/2014/Software_compartmentalization_vs_physical_separation.pdf>`__."
msgstr ""
"面對這個發人深省的現實，Qubes 採取了一種極為務實的方法：限制、控制並遏制損"
"害。它讓您可以將寶貴的資料與風險活動分開，防止交叉污染。這意味著您可以在同一"
"台實體電腦上完成所有事情，而不必擔心一次成功的網路攻擊就將您的整個數位生活一"
"舉摧毀。事實上，Qubes 相較於實體空氣隔離具有 `明顯的優勢 <https://"
"invisiblethingslab.com/resources/2014/"
"Software_compartmentalization_vs_physical_separation.pdf>`__。"

#: ../../../introduction/intro.rst:118 30fec73e6f5747f393d668597d06261c
msgid "Compartmentalization example"
msgstr "隔間化範例"

#: ../../../introduction/intro.rst:122 c13a8a4491b945dbb0533fea4c98e81e
msgid "Made to support vulnerable users and power users alike"
msgstr "旨在同時支援弱勢使用者與進階使用者"

#: ../../../introduction/intro.rst:124 05310b502a584899a88bb273c9baad41
msgid ""
"Qubes provides practical, usable security to vulnerable and actively-"
"targeted individuals, such as journalists, activists, whistleblowers, and "
"researchers. Qubes is designed with the understanding that people make "
"mistakes, and it allows you to protect yourself from your own mistakes. It's "
"a place where you can click on links, open attachments, plug in devices, and "
"install software free from worry. It's a place where **you** have control "
"over your software, not the other way around. (See some :doc:`examples of "
"how different types of users organize their qubes </user/how-to-guides/how-"
"to-organize-your-qubes>`.)"
msgstr ""
"Qubes 為弱勢及受主動攻擊目標的個人提供實用、可用的安全性，例如記者、社運人"
"士、吹哨者和研究人員。Qubes 的設計理念認識到人會犯錯，並讓您能夠保護自己免受"
"自身錯誤的影響。在這裡，您可以放心地點擊連結、開啟附件、插入裝置和安裝軟體。"
"在這裡，\\ **您**\\ 掌控您的軟體，而不是反過來被軟體掌控。（請參閱一些 :doc:`"
"不同類型使用者如何組織其 qube 的範例 </user/how-to-guides/how-to-organize-"
"your-qubes>`。）"

#: ../../../introduction/intro.rst:133 6c8f668b294e4c60b27270ed1b8a28a0
msgid ""
"Qubes is also powerful. Organizations like the `Freedom of the Press "
"Foundation <https://securedrop.org/news/piloting-securedrop-workstation-"
"qubes-os>`__, `Mullvad <https://x.com/mullvadnet/"
"status/631010362083643392>`__, and `Let's Encrypt <https://x.com/letsencrypt/"
"status/1239934557710737410>`__ rely on Qubes as they build and maintain "
"critical privacy and security internet technologies that are in turn relied "
"upon by countless users around the world every day. Renowned security "
"`experts <https://qubes-os.org/endorsements/>`__ like Edward Snowden, Daniel "
"J. Bernstein, Micah Lee, Christopher Soghoian, Isis Agora Lovecruft, Peter "
"Todd, Bill Budington, and Kenn White use and recommend Qubes."
msgstr ""
"Qubes 也非常強大。像 `新聞自由基金會 <https://securedrop.org/news/piloting-"
"securedrop-workstation-qubes-os>`__、`Mullvad <https://x.com/mullvadnet/"
"status/631010362083643392>`__ 和 `Let's Encrypt <https://x.com/letsencrypt/"
"status/1239934557710737410>`__ 等組織，在建置和維護關鍵的隱私與安全網際網路技"
"術時都依賴 Qubes，而這些技術每天又被全球無數使用者所依賴。著名的安全 `專家 "
"<https://qubes-os.org/endorsements/>`__ 如 Edward Snowden、Daniel J. "
"Bernstein、Micah Lee、Christopher Soghoian、Isis Agora Lovecruft、Peter "
"Todd、Bill Budington 和 Kenn White 都使用並推薦 Qubes。"

#: ../../../introduction/intro.rst:142 2cae4380b0c74a57b1b442853cb26399
msgid ""
"Qubes is one of the few operating systems that places the security of its "
"users above all else. It is, and always will be, free and open-source "
"software, because the fundamental operating system that constitutes the core "
"infrastructure of our digital lives **must** be free and open-source in "
"order to be trustworthy."
msgstr ""
"Qubes 是少數將使用者安全置於一切之上的作業系統之一。它現在是、也將永遠是自由"
"且開源的軟體，因為構成我們數位生活核心基礎架構的基本作業系統\\ **必須**\\ 是"
"自由且開源的，才能值得信賴。"

